# Theme shows the design system

`joined-theme` is the catalog for `sid-ui`. The component source lives in https://github.com/sid0709/sid-ui, not in this repo. A change to a component, glyph, token, or visual treatment is not done until this theme shows the published look and the `sid-ui` catalog pin matches that release.

When `sid-ui` changes:

1. Update the matching demo in `joined-theme/components/demos/`.
2. Add a new public component to `joined-theme/lib/catalog.ts` and register its demo in `joined-theme/components/demos/load.ts`.
3. Rewrite demo and catalog copy that still describes the old treatment (radius, sizes, icon weight).
4. Bump the `sid-ui` pin in the root catalog.

Glyphs have their own page (`glyph`). A new or redrawn icon is shown there in the same change.

## Tokens

Token values are defined in the sid-ui package. Components and demos use `var(--color-*)`, `var(--spacing-*)`, `var(--radius-*)`, and `var(--font-*)`.

A new visual value is a named token in sid-ui, then a theme demo. No hex, rgb, or raw font size in a component or demo file.

```tsx
// ❌ design system only
// sid-ui Glyph.tsx gained `sun`

// ✅ same change also updates the theme
// joined-theme/components/demos/glyph.tsx renders <Glyph name="sun" />
```
